hls: export the live window when the input ends

The live window is exported after each packet, so the reload that ends the
input never reached it: a playlist that gets EXT-X-ENDLIST without a new
segment ends with hls_finished still 0, and a caller cannot tell it from a
live playlist that stopped growing (m3u8_hold_counters). Export the window
before returning EOF too.

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
index 7add69b..ec413c0 100644
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -3235,6 +3235,11 @@ static int hls_read_packet(AVFormatContext *s, AVPacket *pkt)
         update_live_window(c);
         return 0;
     }
+    /* The reload that ends the input (EXT-X-ENDLIST without a new segment, or
+     * m3u8_hold_counters reloads without one) returns no packet: export the
+     * window it left, so a caller can tell an ended playlist from a live one
+     * that stopped. */
+    update_live_window(c);
     return AVERROR_EOF;
 }
 
